# Port and NIF: measure the boundary

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:swi_elixir, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)},
  {:kino, "== 0.19.0"}
])
```

## Introduction

Port runs SWI in a separate process; NIF embeds it in the BEAM VM. Both use
the same loading, calling, and streaming API. This chapter measures startup
and repeated operations, then demonstrates timeout and crash recovery.
The theorem workloads use [leanHaT](https://leancop.de/leanhat/) and
[nanoCoP-i-HT](https://www.leancop.de/ihat/).

Start with [Getting started](01_basic.livemd) if session ownership is new to
you. Evaluate top to bottom in a runtime on a [supported platform](../README.md#platforms-and-native-bundles).
Setup installs this checkout, its bundled SWI runtime, and Kino. Results are measured on your machine;
this is a local boundary comparison, not a solver ranking.

[All chapters](intro.livemd).

